  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000019: nn_2opt\n\nStatus: valid; distance: 17.634\n\nThought: Construct initial tour using nearest neighbor heuristic to quickly produce a valid tour, then apply 2-opt improvement until budget exhausted. Nearest neighbor is simple and robust, and 2-opt effectively reduces crossings.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray, seed: int, budget: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    n = distance_matrix.shape[0]\n    if n <= 2:\n        return np.arange(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    # Nearest neighbor construction\n    start = np.random.randint(n)\n    tour = [start]\n    unvisited = set(range(n))\n    unvisited.remove(start)\n    last = start\n    while unvisited:\n        best_dist = float('inf')\n        best_city = -1\n        for city in unvisited:\n            d = distance_matrix[last, city]\n            if d < best_dist:\n                best_dist = d\n                best_city = city\n        tour.append(best_city)\n        unvisited.remove(best_city)\n        last = best_city\n    tour = np.array(tour, dtype=np.int32)\n    total = sum(distance_matrix[tour[i], tour[(i+1)%n]] for i in range(n))\n    best_tour = tour.copy()\n    best_dist = total\n    report_best_tour(best_tour)\n    # 2-opt improvement\n    iteration = 0\n    improved = True\n    while improved and iteration < budget:\n        improved = False\n        for i in range(n-2):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                if iteration >= budget:\n                    break\n                a, b, c, d = tour[i], tour[i+1], tour[j], tour[(j+1)%n]\n                delta = distance_matrix[a, c] + distance_matrix[b, d] - distance_matrix[a, b] - distance_matrix[c, d]\n                if delta < -1e-12:\n                    tour[i+1:j+1] = tour[i+1:j+1][::-1]\n                    total += delta\n                    if total < best_dist - 1e-12:\n                        best_dist = total\n                        best_tour = tour.copy()\n                        report_best_tour(best_tour)\n                    improved = True\n                    break\n            if improved or iteration >= budget:\n                break\n        iteration += 1\n    return best_tour\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000005 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Randomized greedy + 2-opt achieved good 500-city results; mean distance 32.84 with fast runtime and no invalid tours.\n- Aim: Improve construction heuristic to produce higher-quality starting tours, reducing tour length without exceeding budget.\n- Preserve: budget-aware 2-opt loop; valid permutation guarantee; report_best_tour mechanism; fast runtime profile\n- Change: replace randomized greedy with nearest insertion or regret-based construction; add a simple perturbation restart if time allows within budget\n- Avoid: introducing invalid tours; increasing runtime beyond budget tolerance; unnecessary complexity that does not reduce tour length; breaking the 2-opt core correctness\n\nDistance is the search objective for TSP; lower distance is better.\n\nImplement this function only:\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray, seed: int, budget: int) -> np.ndarray:\n\nRequirements:\n- Minimize total TSP tour distance.\n- Return a 1D np.ndarray containing each node exactly once.\n- Do not repeat the start node at the end.\n- Always return a valid tour, even when budget is very small.\n- Use only distance_matrix; do not assume coordinates.\n- Use seed for randomness.\n- Treat budget as a hard cap on search effort.\n- Create a valid tour early.\n- Call report_best_tour(tour) whenever a new best valid tour is found, assume this func already exists.\n- Do not use files, network, subprocesses, or external solvers.\n- Keep the code compact and robust.\n\ncorrect signature, valid tour on every return path,\nearly report_best_tour, budget-bounded main search, allowed imports only, no I/O/network/subprocesses.\n\nReturn one JSON object and nothing else:\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"short_snake_case_name\",\n  \"thought\": \"high-level summary of the construction, improvement, and tie-break logic\",\n  \"code\": \"complete Python code as a JSON string\"\n}\nNo Markdown, fences, or text outside JSON. The code string must define solve_tsp.",
